<title>FINLAND: Nokia rises post-Motorola Q2.</title>
<headline>Nokia rises post-Motorola Q2.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish telecoms group Nokia Oy rose sharply on Wednesday, drawing strength from overnight gains on Wall Street and U.S. rival Motorola 's above-forecast Q2 earnings after NYSE's close, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1120/0820 GMT, Nokia traded at 426.00 markka, up 13.50 markka or 3.3 percent, after setting a new life-high of 431.00 in fairly lively 80 million markka trade.</p>
<p>Overall bourse sentiment was bullish as forestry stocks rose sharply, and though some analysts said Motorola's report did not as such contain much good news for Nokia, they expected gains in Motorola to boost interest in Nokia.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
